# Raw stores stay out of git; COMPACT BUNDLES go in. The distinction is size and
# reproducibility, not principle. candles/ is ~1.2GB of minute bars and is regenerable
# from the exchange; candle-bundle/ is ~9MB of daily bars and is NOT -- Kraken's public
# OHLC endpoint returns only 720 rows, so a lost bundle cannot be re-pulled, only
# rebuilt from a raw store that exists on one machine.
# It was excluded here until 2026-09-10, when a container restart destroyed it along
# with the uploads directory and took 18 tests down with it. sp500-bundle (11M),
# candle-bundle-long (4.3M) and funding-binance (5.8M) were already tracked, so this
# rule was the only thing standing between the crypto universe and permanence.
candle-bundle.tar.gz
